559 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 227 0 R /Rect [ 63.699001 512.405978 531.458984 756.245974 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure3) /TU (Composite data visualization with three panels compares Legal-BERT, CaseLawBERT, BERT-base, and GPT-3.5 on legal text extraction. Top left: boxplot displays span-level F1 scores for each model, showing Legal-BERT and CaseLawBERT outperforming others. Top right: heatmap shows IoU scores by clause type and model, with Legal-BERT achieving highest values across all clause types. Bottom: stacked bar chart depicts error proportions by type\204partial match, boundary shift, and missed\204for each model, indicating increasing total error from Legal-BERT to GPT-3.5.) /Type /Annot >>
