663 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart showing the process from private sector contracts through document classification and clause extraction, leading to new regulation and summary generation, with language models BERT, Legal-BERT, and T5 supporting classification and summarization.) /K 718 0 R /P 235 0 R /Pg 222 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
664 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Four data visualizations compare five language models: BERT-base, GPT-3.5, Legal-BERT, CaseLawBERT, and LoRA-Legal-BERT. Panel A displays Macro-F1 variability across 20 runs using box plots. Panel B shows bar charts of average Macro-F1 scores annotated with model sizes. Panel C presents a bar chart of Macro-F1 improvement over BERT-base. Panel D features a heatmap indicating correlation coefficients between Macro-F1, ROC-AUC, and log-transformed parameter size.) /K 719 0 R /P 235 0 R /Pg 225 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
665 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Composite data visualization with three panels compares Legal-BERT, CaseLawBERT, BERT-base, and GPT-3.5 on legal text extraction. Top left: boxplot displays span-level F1 scores for each model, showing Legal-BERT and CaseLawBERT outperforming others. Top right: heatmap shows IoU scores by clause type and model, with Legal-BERT achieving highest values across all clause types. Bottom: stacked bar chart depicts error proportions by type\204partial match, boundary shift, and missed\204for each model, indicating increasing total error from Legal-BERT to GPT-3.5.) /K 720 0 R /P 235 0 R /Pg 227 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
666 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Three data visualizations show text model performance: \(A\) a heatmap comparing ROUGE-1, ROUGE-2, and ROUGE-L scores for six models; \(B\) a scatter plot of BLEU versus BERTScore for the same models; \(C\) a horizontal bar chart ranking models by average metric, where lower is better.) /K 721 0 R /P 235 0 R /Pg 228 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
667 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Heatmap comparing the performance of BERT, GPT-3.5, GPT-4, and LegalBERT across Macro-F1, Span-F1, and ROUGE-L metrics, where GPT-4 achieves the highest scores in all metrics, ranging from 0.88 to 0.91. Color bar on the right indicates score range from zero to one.) /K 722 0 R /P 235 0 R /Pg 229 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
668 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Violin plot with three panels comparing five models\204BERT, LegalBERT, CaseLawBERT, GPT-2 \(Large\), and GPT-3.5\204across Macro-F1, Span-F1, and ROUGE-L metrics. Each panel shows distribution shapes and summary statistics, visually indicating model performance variability and central tendency for each metric.) /K 723 0 R /P 235 0 R /Pg 230 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
